{
 "meta": {
  "proposal": "ng_brain s101.0 - TIER 3 DOCTRINE (DATA_GATE_S98 items 1-5)",
  "status": "PROPOSAL - printed to Greg 2026-07-20 (S100); NOTHING merged into ng_brain.json until his approval (standing protocol)",
  "scope_note": "ALL items are GUIDANCE/METHOD/BOOKKEEPING the agent reads - never gates, never play changes; C1-C4 and every existing play stay byte-identical."
 },
 "usage_doctrine": {
  "note": "Per-source-family READING guidance (gate item 1). How to read each family - the agent decides application.",
  "weather_mos": "FIRST-APPEARANCE adds at previously-empty horizons are the driver class; REVISIONS to already-priced horizons are the noise class (s100_2_mos_characterization, n thin - forward evidence rides G12+). D+4-8 = the battleground horizons where repricing concentrates. The weekend 00z/12z cycles price the SUNDAY REOPEN - weather_forecast_cycle (feed A ph1) carries them decision-time; the D-1-evening block alone is one cycle behind every reopen. freeze_risk (feed E) is the SUPPLY side of cold: sub-20F producing-basin runs cut supply while demand spikes - the convexity mechanism behind band overshoots.",
  "storage": "The weekly print RE-ANCHORS the fundamental backdrop; it never owns the day side (prints trade chain-sided at current polarity, 9/9 through G11). SALT is the fast-cycling front-month scarcity read; composition (regional vs headline) is the second wave. Survey consensus and seasonal proxy are BOTH carried - surprise is vs consensus where consensus exists.",
  "cot": "Positioning is a CONVEXITY CONDITIONER, never timing or direction. Percentile extremes flag band-overshoot regimes (squeezes overshoot every band). NEVER fade the crowded side during its squeeze. Limits: weekly cadence, Tuesday-positions-Friday-publication, and the futures book and options-implied book can sit at OPPOSITE extremes (G11 open: 2.83rd vs 97.17th pctile) - read BOTH.",
  "structure": "Curve LEVEL is state; the widening RATE is signal. The expiry clock switches the regime (squeeze_watch active = delivery physics) - and only the CALENDAR-FRONT fields see it (the OI-front hides the squeeze; 0122: 0.093 vs 1.539). squeeze_watch is a read, not a gate.",
  "vol": "vol_regime scales BANDS only, never calls direction. n0/v0 bases never mixed.",
  "options": "OI walls = the pin map near opex (pin/unpin boundary = opex day, the business day before expiry). Wall concentrations near settle act as magnets/friction zones. IV (phase ii, pending) = uncertainty scaler, never direction.",
  "power_solar_nuclear_grid": "Slow demand-share backdrop + the daily burn nowcast (grid_stack); nuclear GW offline adds burn ~GW-for-GW; the sunset ramp (solar_calendar) is an intraday clock feature, not a daily driver.",
  "cash": "Cash basis is delivery-stress GROUND TRUTH the paper market converges to - but it publishes in WEEKLY BATCHES; never assume daily availability (the 0130 +10.77 lands decision-time-legit ON the 17x day, not before)."
 },
 "flip_driver_checklist": {
  "note": "Gate item 2 (desk review B2). METHOD, joins C1-C4 which stay unchanged: at EVERY chain_polarity_flip ARM or CONFIRM evaluation the agent must READ (not obey) all four families before deciding.",
  "checklist": [
   "FORECAST STREAM: any first-appearance adds? which side do they feed? (weather_forecast run_delta + weather_forecast_cycle deltas + freeze_risk threshold crossings)",
   "POSITIONING: COT percentile + WHICH book (futures vs options-implied) is at an extreme; is the flip direction the crowded side's squeeze?",
   "STRUCTURE: calendar-front spread level AND its widening rate; days to calendar-front expiry; squeeze_watch state",
   "TAPE: C1 band-break state vs the correct condition-class band; C2 arms where in scope (per s100_3 scoping)"
  ],
  "rule": "The checklist forces the LOOK; the confirm bar (C1+C3+C4, C2 in scope) still DECIDES. No checklist item is itself a confirm condition."
 },
